# Neo Gate parameters (docs/specs/mastering-tools.md §5.13). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoGate
namespace NeoBuzz.Gate
class NeoGateMachine
summary Noise gate and downward expander, the successor of Pedal Gate: a threshold with a separate, lower close threshold (hysteresis), attack, hold and release (linear gain ramps, as Pedal Gate's), a Range floor, an expansion ratio (infinity is a hard gate, lower ratios expand downwards), Peak or RMS detection, a key filter (low and high cut), an external sidechain on input 2, lookahead and Listen to the key. Delta (hear only what the gate takes out) and a gain-match reading. Use it to clean spill from drum tracks, tighten a bass or cut the noise between phrases.

group Gate
Threshold  "Threshold"     0 1000 625   lin -80 0 dB 1                    | The level that opens the gate
Hysteresis "Hysteresis"    0 1000 300   lin 0 20 dB 1                     | The gate closes this far under the threshold: more means less chatter
Ratio      "Ratio"         0 1000 1000  ratio 1 20 inf                    | Expansion below the close threshold: every dB under it is (ratio − 1) dB quieter, down to Range. Infinity: a hard gate that goes straight to Range
Range      "Range"         0 90    0    lin -90 0 dB 0                    | The closed gate's gain floor: -90 dB nearly shut, 0 dB no gating
group Timing
Attack     "Attack"        0 1000  459  time 0.0001 0.5                   | Time for the gain to open fully (a linear ramp)
Hold       "Hold"          0 1000  606  time 0.001 2                      | How long the gate stays open after the signal falls under the close threshold
Release    "Release"       0 1000  697  time 0.001 2                      | Time for the gain to close fully (a linear ramp)
Lookahead  "Lookahead"     0 1000  0    lin 0 25 ms 1                     | Delays the audio so the gate opens before the transient arrives (latency)
group Key
Detection  "Detection"     0 1     0    enum Peak RMS                     | Peak: fast, follows transients. RMS: 10 ms average, smoother on sustained sources
Sidechain  "Sidechain"     0 1     0    enum Internal External            | Detect from the input, or from input 2 (connect a machine to the second input)
KeyLow     "Key low cut"   0 1000  0    freq 10 2000                      | High-pass on the key: keeps low rumble from opening the gate (off at its minimum)
KeyHigh    "Key high cut"  0 1000  1000 freq 1000 22000                   | Low-pass on the key: keeps hiss and cymbals from opening the gate (off at its maximum)
Listen     "Listen"        0 1     0    switch                            | Hear the key signal, filtered
group Output
Output     "Output"        0 480   240  db -24 24                         | Gain after the gate, 0.1 dB steps (the editor's Match sets it from the gain-match reading)
Delta      "Delta"         0 1     0    switch                            | Hear only what the gate takes out: the output minus the input, delayed to match (glides over 10 ms)

# What the gate measures (NeoGateMachine.Readings, machine_readings).
reading gain_db           dB    | The gate's gain now, dB (0 open, down to Range when closed)
reading open              flag  | 1 while the gate is open, 0 while it is closed or closing
reading gain_match_db     dB    | Short-term loudness out − in (K-weighted, 3 s)
reading latency_samples   samples | The lookahead, reported to NeoBuzz Live
